[claude:event system] {"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"bv5l1blwc","tool_use_id":"toolu_012w2MhM9cUvunvZshGnxRuM","description":"\npython3 << 'EOF'\ndef read_ppm(filename):\n    with open(filename, 'r') as f:\n        f.readline()\n        dims = f.readline().strip().split()\n        width, height = int(dims[0]), int(dims[1])\n        f.readline()\n        pixels = []\n        for line in f:\n            line = line.strip()\n            if line:\n                r, g, b = map(int, line.split())\n                pixels.append((r, g, b))\n    return width, height, pixels\n\nw, h, pixels = read_ppm('/app/image.ppm')\n\n# Find the red stripe boundaries\n# Check row 900 to see the x range of the red stripe\nprint(\"Row 900 - looking for red stripe:\")\ny = 900\nfor x in range(1000, 1400, 10):\n    r, g, b = pixels[y * w + x]\n    print(f\"  x={x:4d}: ({r:3d}, {g:3d}, {b:3d})\", end=\"\")\n    if r > 40 and g < 20:\n        print(\" <- RED\")\n    else:\n        print()\n\n# Find boundaries precisely\nprint(\"\\nRow 900 - exact red stripe boundaries:\")\ny = 900\nfor x in range(1050, 1350):\n    r, g, b = pixels[y * w + x]\n    if (r < 200 and g < 50):  # Reddish\n        print(f\"x={x}: ({r}, {g}, {b})\")\n\nEOF\n","is_backgrounded":false,"task_type":"local_bash","uuid":"ef75f32d-ede2-4227-a0d3-d3589da71a29","session_id":"d8dadbad-fa41-49c6-8f50-bf9dbcbeed9a"}
