[claude:event system] {"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"bio0g2u8n","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jb3UjZTMrCdyUJAPpoUsbw","description":"\ngcc -static -o image image.c -lm && ./image && python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\ndef read_ppm(filename):\n    with open(filename, 'r') as f:\n        f.readline()\n        f.readline()\n        f.readline()\n        pixels = []\n        for line in f:\n            line = line.strip()\n            if line:\n                r, g, b = map(int, line.split())\n                pixels.append((r, g, b))\n    return pixels\n\npixels_orig = read_ppm('/app/image.ppm')\npixels_recon = read_ppm('/app/reconstructed.ppm')\n\ndot_prod = 0\nnorm_sq_orig = 0\nnorm_sq_recon = 0\n\nfor (r1, g1, b1), (r2, g2, b2) in zip(pixels_orig, pixels_recon):\n    norm_sq_orig += r1*r1 + g1*g1 + b1*b1\n    norm_sq_recon += r2*r2 + g2*g2 + b2*b2\n    dot_prod += r1*r2 + g1*g2 + b1*b2\n\ncos_sim = dot_prod / (math.sqrt(norm_sq_orig) * math.sqrt(norm_sq_recon))\nprint(f\"Cosine similarity: {cos_sim:.6f}\")\n\n# Also compute file size\nimport os\nsize = os.path.getsize('/app/image.c')\nprint(f\"File size: {size} bytes\")\n\nEOF\n","is_backgrounded":false,"task_type":"local_bash","uuid":"b530d94d-7476-45b8-b195-45a2d8adddef","session_id":"d8dadbad-fa41-49c6-8f50-bf9dbcbeed9a"}
